# Progethod

A simplified timesheet interface for Wethod. Data is stored locally (localStorage) and synced to a backend API. Built with Nuxt 4 (SPA mode, static preset) + Pinia 4 + Tailwind CSS 4.

## Architecture

- **Framework**: Nuxt 4 (Vue 3.5), SPA mode (`ssr: false`, Nitro preset `static`)
- **State**: Pinia 4 stores persisted to localStorage via custom plugin (`plugins/persistence.client.ts`)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4 via `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin (CSS-first config in `assets/css/tailwind.css`)
- **i18n**: `@nuxtjs/i18n` v10 (vue-i18n v11), Italian only (`locales/it.json`)
- **API**: `$fetch` wrapped in `composables/useApi.ts`, backend at `/api/`
- **Calendar**: Google Calendar integration for importing events. GAPI (`apis.google.com/js/api.js`) and GIS (`accounts.google.com/gsi/client`) scripts loaded via `app.head` in `nuxt.config.ts`. `utils/gCal.ts` waits for scripts before using `window.gapi`/`window.google`. Auth: try silent GIS token refresh first; on failure or API 401/403, invalidate local expiry, clear `gapi.client` token, and re-prompt with `prompt: 'consent'` so the user can log in again without refreshing the page. Token expiry is session-only (not persisted); live auth also requires a present `gapi.client` access token. Imported event durations are rounded **up** via `roundDurationMinutes` (`utils/duration.ts`) using `preferences.durationRoundingMinutes` (0 = no rounding, 15, 30; user-menu segmented picker, default 15). The preference is generic (not calendar-specific) so other integrations can reuse the same transform.
- **Magic Tags**: Format `[progethod:{wethodProjectId}:{areaId|generic}]` (`utils/magicTag.ts`). On calendar import, prefer a local shortcut with matching `linkedProjectId`/`linkedAreaId`; else set `directWethodProjectId`/`directWethodAreaId` if that Wethod project+area is in the cached `apiData` board; else leave the entry unassigned (never invent ids missing from cache). Copy from local project config, or from `MagicTagLookup` on the Progetti page (Wethod project/area → tag, no shortcut required).
- **Jira**: OAuth 2.0 + PKCE popup flow to fetch daily Jira activity (tickets touched that day)
- **GitLab**: OAuth 2.0 + PKCE popup flow to fetch daily GitLab commits (push events). Activity endpoint (`functions/api/gitlab-activity.js`): round 1 fetches push events (±1d UTC window — `/events` only accepts UTC dates, so the net is wide and results are filtered to the local day via the client-sent `tz` offset; extra pages fetched in parallel, capped by `MAX_EVENT_PAGES`) in parallel with `/user` + `/user/emails`; round 2 lists each pushed branch's day commits via `commits?ref_name=&since=&until=` (one cheap call per project+ref) plus one `GET /projects/:id` per project for path/name. **Never use the compare API here** — it computes the full file diff we never display and made the modal take 30-40s (Sept 2026). Trade-off: commits authored before that day that entered the branch via the push (e.g. merging an old branch) are not listed. Commits are filtered to the user's own (author email ∈ user emails, or author name = name/username). All round-2 calls run through a shared concurrency pool (`REQUEST_CONCURRENCY = 6`). Client-side, `utils/gitlab.ts` shares in-flight requests per day (not a cache — settled results are dropped) so the hover/focus prefetch on the day-row GitLab button and the modal open share one request; prefetch never triggers token refresh or the OAuth popup.
- **PWA**: `@vite-pwa/nuxt` v1
- **Build**: `nuxt generate` outputs to `.output/public/`, deployed to Cloudflare Pages
- **Node**: 22 LTS (via Volta)

## Pinia Stores

- `stores/softDeletableStore.ts` — Factory composable (`useSoftDeletableCollection<T>`) providing shared CRUD + soft-delete logic (items ref, updatedAt ref, visibleItems computed, add/update/remove/restoreBackup/restoreFromServer). Used by projects and presets stores.
- `stores/projects.ts` — User-created local project shortcuts (aliases to Wethod projects/areas). Setup store using `useSoftDeletableCollection<Project>`, adds `removeMany` and `markUpToDate`.
- `stores/presets.ts` — User-created note presets shown when the notes field is empty. Setup store using `useSoftDeletableCollection<Preset>`, adds `reorder`.
- `stores/entries.ts` — Daily timesheet entries
- `stores/user.ts` — Auth token, user info, integration tokens (Jira, GitLab, GCal)
- `stores/apiData.ts` — Cached Wethod project data
- `stores/preferences.ts` — UI preferences (confirm on submit, business unit filter, theme, high contrast, duration rounding, temporary `weekLayout` A/B)

## Composables

- `composables/useApi.ts` — API client wrapping `$fetch` with auth headers and 401 handling
- `composables/useEventBus.ts` — Cross-component event bus using `mitt`
- `composables/useLiveToday.ts` — Reactive `today` ref that updates at midnight
- `composables/useModalKeyboard.ts` — Shared Escape/Enter handling for modals; tracks open modal count via `useHasOpenModal()` so global shortcuts yield

## Key Decisions

- **Week layout A/B**: Temporary experiment. Three layouts under `components/ab-week-layouts/` (`classic` / `rail` / `split`), selected via user menu → “Vista settimana”, persisted as `preferences.weekLayout`. Delete that folder (and preference/menu/i18n hooks) when a winner is chosen — see the folder README.
- **Business unit filter**: Compact navbar cell (`BU` + `selected/total`) left of the session status cell, with a shared left tray divider. Click opens an animated dropdown with search, select-all, and multi-select; hint suggests selecting your own BU and Corporate. Also in the mobile menu (`variant="menu"`). Selection is in `preferences.selectedBusinessUnitIds` and applied as `bu=` on project refresh / Wethod hours detail. Session status uses a key + green/red dot; its menu shows “Copia token Wethod” only when `canMakeRequests`, otherwise a non-clickable reauth hint (`session_expired` / `session_expired_hint`). Same on mobile. Nav menus (status / BU / profile) are mutually exclusive via `nav-menu:open`.
- **Note presets**: Global note presets (not project-scoped). Appear only when notes field is focused + empty. Keyboard navigation: ArrowDown enters presets mode, ArrowLeft/Right navigates, Enter selects, ArrowUp/Esc exits. Stored same as projects with soft-delete pattern. Backend API endpoint remains `pills` for backward compatibility.
- **Persistence**: All Pinia stores persisted to localStorage under the key `progethod`. Migration from old `vuex` key happens automatically on first load. Soft-deleted items pruned after 40 days. Hydration lives in `utils/persistedState.ts` (shared by the persistence plugin and backup restore). Restore writes the file as-is to localStorage and hydrates Pinia in place (no full reload); persistence saves are suppressed during that swap so storage is not briefly wiped.
- **Sync**: Projects and presets sync to backend via PUT on mutation (`plugins/sync.client.ts`). Entries are local-only until explicitly submitted.
- **Keyboard navigation**: Full keyboard nav via `plugins/keyboard-shortcuts.client.ts`. Global shortcuts only fire when user is not typing in an input, and are fully suppressed while a modal is open (`useHasOpenModal`).
- **Modal keyboard**: All modals use `useModalKeyboard` (via `Modal.vue` or directly) with capture-phase `window` listeners so keys work even when focus is still on the opener. Escape always dismisses. Enter confirms only when `Modal` has `confirmable` (or `onConfirm` is passed). Enter is skipped in textareas and on focused controls *inside* the modal (`[data-modal-overlay]`), so Cancel/Delete/Retry keep native behaviour. Informational modals (office days, Wethod hours, guide, shortcuts help) are Escape-only.
- **External integrations (Jira/GitLab)**: Same pattern — OAuth popup with PKCE, server-side token exchange via Cloudflare Pages Function, activity proxy, modal UI. Tokens stored in `user` Pinia store with expiration. Auth routes bypass the main auth middleware. Both token exchange endpoints use server-side env vars (`*_CLIENT_SECRET`) while client-side only exposes `*_CLIENT_ID` via `runtimeConfig.public`. Refresh tokens are persisted alongside access tokens; when an access token expires, the client silently refreshes via the same server-side endpoint (`grant_type: refresh_token`) before falling back to the full OAuth popup flow. Jira rotates refresh tokens on each use (new one returned and stored).
- **Month stats reference date**: Month label, tracked days, working days, and office days are computed from `weekAnchor` (= today + weekOffset), not from `days[0]` (Monday of the week). This ensures that when a week spans two months, the stats reflect the month the user is "anchored to" (i.e. today's month for the current week).
- **Office days**: Sourced from Wethod, not local entries. No monthly target/pace UI (targets vary: 8/12/16). Client fans out single-day checks in parallel (`CHECK_CONCURRENCY = 6`) against `/api/office-days?date=&expected=&bu=`, with a progress bar. Uses the same BU filter as project refresh / Wethod hours detail so the board is much smaller (usually 1 page). Each call paginates `timetrackingboard` via `fetchTimetrackingBoardPages`, sums non-automatic `internal` hours, and treats `>= 8` as an office day. Early-stop when `internal >= 8` or work hours reach that day's tracked total. Caveat: hours on projects outside the selected BUs are invisible (same as hours modal). Modal shows count + matched dates. In Wethod's data model, `internal` = office, `remote` = home.
- **Theming**: 4-mode system — light, dark, light+high-contrast, dark+high-contrast. Colors are defined as semantic CSS custom properties in `assets/css/theme.css` and registered as Tailwind utilities via `@theme inline` in `assets/css/tailwind.css`. Palette layers cascade via `.dark` and `.high-contrast` classes on `<html>`. Base themes are colorblind-safe (emerald for success, not pure green). High contrast targets WCAG AAA. Theme preference (`auto`/`light`/`dark`) and `highContrast` boolean are stored in `stores/preferences.ts`. `plugins/theme.client.ts` applies classes to `<html>` and listens to `prefers-color-scheme` for auto mode. Settings UI lives in the user dropdown menu in `layouts/default.vue`. Integration brand colors use `--color-gcal` / `--color-jira` / `--color-gitlab` (with HC variants); light values are AA-tuned rather than raw official hex. Raised surfaces (day cards, dark project/preset cards) use `--color-card-raised` (HC maps to `card-hover`). No component should use hardcoded color classes — always use semantic tokens (`text-ink`, `bg-card`, `border-stroke`, `text-accent-fg`, etc.). Style blocks using `@apply` must include `@reference "~/assets/css/tailwind.css"` at the top.
- **Selected / active accent fills**: Solid selected states (theme chips, sidebar Prossime/Storico tabs, on toggles, leave type P/F pills, timesheet location chips, project/preset name chips) use `bg-accent` + `text-ink-inverse` in every theme. Location no longer has a separate palette — it uses accent. Soft accent (`bg-accent-soft` / `text-accent-fg`) remains for quieter highlights (hover rows, bordered chips like HoursPerDayPicker / note presets, focus washes, calendar selection).
- **Stale / warning highlight**: When a project shortcut is missing on Wethod, highlight via warning border + soft warning background + warning text — never `opacity-*` on the whole card (that washes out the accent chip and reads as a chip color change).
- **UI sizing / focus**: Minimum readable text is `text-xs` (12px) — avoid `text-[10px]`/`text-[11px]`. Interactive controls target ≥24×24px (`min-w-6 min-h-6` or larger). Focus indicators use `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-focus-ring` (no resting-state visual change). Hover-only actions (sidebar edit/delete, Jira/GitLab copy) also reveal on `:focus-within` / `focus-visible`.
- **Typography (DM Sans)**: Global `letter-spacing: 0.01em`, `font-optical-sizing: auto`, `opsz` 14, and antialiased rendering to reduce letter blending on dark UI. Prefer `font-semibold` over `font-bold` at `text-xs`; small text gets `0.015em` tracking.
- **Holidays**: Fetched from `/api/holidays` (Factorial iCal proxy). Holidays are excluded from calendar interactions the same way weekends are (non-clickable, non-selectable in drag). Displayed in MonthCalendar widget with disabled styling. On main weekly timesheet, holidays render as a badge on the day stat bar. Data is `[{ date, name }]`.
- **Reusable UI components**: Prefer shared presentational components with props/slots over copy-pasted markup.
  - `LogoBrand` — CSS 3D matte extruded accent wordmark (layered spans + anime.js idle tumble). Defaults to “Progethod” at `lg+` and compact “P” below; force with `wordless` / `responsive`. Fitted so the tilt stays inside the 64px nav; `prefers-reduced-motion` skips motion.
  - `DayStatBadge` — day/month status chips (border tint only)
  - `PanelModal` — shared panel shell (guide, shortcuts, Jira/GitLab pickers). Default chrome: `max-w-lg`, `max-h-[85vh]`, `px-6 pt-6 pb-4` header, `text-lg` title. Only override when needed (e.g. shortcuts `max-w-md`).
  - `ActivityPickerModal` — search + grouped selectable list; thin `JiraActivityModal` / `GitlabActivityModal` wrappers own fetch + item slots
  - `IconButton`, `ToggleSwitch`; `LoadingState` / `ErrorState` use one accent-spinner style everywhere
  - Leave UI: `LeaveTypePill`, `LeaveTypeToggle`, `HoursPerDayPicker`, `SidebarRequestRow`, `RequestStatusBadge` + `utils/leaveStatus.ts`. Type pills (F/P) share one accent style (solid `bg-accent` / `text-ink-inverse`) — no color distinction between Ferie and Permesso. Sidebar request rows cluster date+hours on the left (weekday + day, e.g. `ven 10`) and type+status on the right.
  - `utils/calendarGrid.ts` — Monday-first month grid + Italian weekday headers
  - `utils/clipboard.ts` — shared copy helper
  - Duration strings: `formatDurationLabel` / `formatDecimalHoursLabel` in `utils/duration.ts`
- **Leave display (main page)**: Ferie and Permesso are merged into a single "Assenze" badge on the weekly timesheet (`DayInputItem`). They remain separate on the `/ferie` calendar page. Approved leave cells on `/ferie` use accent (not vacation teal) so they don't read as success; pending stays orange. Multi-day selection uses `ring-inset` to avoid outline overlap between adjacent cells.
- **API diagnostic**: "Esegui diagnostica" in the session status menu (desktop + mobile) opens `DiagnosticModal.vue`, which runs every Wethod call the app depends on and validates response shapes (`utils/diagnostics.ts`). Matching is subset-based (extra fields OK, missing/wrong-typed fields fail); Wethod error envelopes (`code !== 200` with HTTP 200, e.g. `route_not_found`) count as failures. Board-based checks (timetrackingboard, office-days, tracked-hours-detail) pass the user's BU filter (`bu=` from preferences) for speed. Read checks run in parallel, write checks sequentially after: allocation-request create → patch → delete (Ferie project 83, 8h, notes "test", first free weekday ≥14 days out) and timetracking write → cleanup (0.1h remote, removed via null-types POST like day reset). The write targets the first `can_edit` project on today's board — leave projects 83/90 are `is_timesheet_automatic`, so they're never writable. Closing the modal never aborts a run so cleanup always completes. Failed rows expand on click with the mismatch paths.
- **Planningboard parsing**: Wethod removed `planningboard/` (Sept 2026, `route_not_found`); leave data now comes from `planning-groups`. Our client-facing `/api/planningboard` route is unchanged — `functions/api/planningboard.js` translates `from`/`to` into Wethod's operator-prefixed overlap filters (`to_date=gte:<from>&from_date=lte:<to>`). The response is a flat company-wide array of multi-day allocations (`person_id`, `project_id`, `daily_minutes`, `dates[]`, `allocation_request_id`, `allocation_request_status`; pending requests appear with status `pending`). Wethod ignores person/project filters (`person_id=`/`project_id=` are no-ops) and returns the company-wide month (~115KB); filtering happens client-side via `filterPlannings` (`employee_id` from userinfo = `person_id`). We still forward `person_id` through the proxy so the payload shrinks automatically if Wethod ever honors it. Don't trim in the proxy — it still has to fetch and parse the full payload anyway. Responses are parsed via `utils/plannings.ts` (`normalizePlanningsResponse` expands `dates[]` into per-day entries, minutes → hours; `filterPlannings`), shared by `pages/ferie.vue` and `pages/index.vue`. It also still tolerates the legacy shape — never parse it inline.
- **Effective Wethod hours**: Shared helper `utils/effectiveHours.ts`: `max(rawWethodHours, syncedLocalHours + leaveHours + holidayHours)`. Wethod folds approved leave into tracked hours once the day arrives — hours land on leave projects 83/90 (`is_timesheet_automatic`, area "generic", bucket `internal`, e.g. "Permessi - ROL [Leaves]") and are included in `tracked-hours`, while the planning board keeps the same allocation. The single `max()` keeps the projection idempotent across that fold (verified 2026-09: 4h approved Permesso Friday → tracked-hours value 4 AND a 4h planning row; adding would double-count). Unsubmitted local entries don't count. Holiday hours = 8 for weekday holidays only. Used by the "Ore su Wethod" badge, week-layout day health, month calendar cell colors, and `monthTrackedDays` (`X/Y`). Leave for the calendar comes from planningboard projects 83/90 for the displayed month (including month navigation); holidays stay excluded/greyed as before. Badge order is [Totale] [Holiday] [Assenze] [Wethod] — Wethod last because it represents the expected sum.
- **Wethod hours breakdown**: Clicking the "Ore su Wethod" day-stat badge opens `WethodHoursModal`, which fetches `/api/tracked-hours-detail` (not the full board). That endpoint paginates `timetrackingboard` via the shared helper, returns only areas with hours > 0, applies the user's BU filter (`bu=` from preferences, same as project refresh), and early-stops once found hours reach the badge total (`expected` from `/api/tracked-hours`). Shows total + per-type chips (office/home/travel/overtime/night_shift) and notes when present.
- **Day reset (NukeTimesheetModal)**: Fetches `timetrackingboard` for the day **with the BU filter** (same as project refresh) to find editable areas to clear — keeps the board to ~1 page. Caveat: entries on projects outside the selected BUs are not cleared. Progress UI: indeterminate bar during the board fetch (single request, no measurable progress), determinate % during the delete posts. Wethod's board response has no total count, so page count is unknowable upfront.
- **Allocation request notes**: System-generated notes matching `Allocation request imported on ...` are stripped when pre-filling the edit modal. The notes field only contains user-authored content.
- **Allocation requests CRUD**: Full CRUD via Cloudflare Pages Functions: `GET/POST` at `allocation-request.js`, `PATCH/DELETE` at `allocation-request/[id].js`. Multi-day drag creates a single request. Multiselect on days with existing requests filters them out, only creating for empty days. Individual day deselection via X button in the create modal. Edit/delete accessible both from calendar cell click and sidebar buttons.
- **Time off budget**: Annual budget overview on the `/ferie` page. Fetches from Wethod's `/timeoff/` endpoint (proxied via `functions/api/timeoff.js`), filters by the current user's `employee_id`. Shows vacation (ferie) and leave (permessi) separately with stacked progress bars (used/planned/requested vs total). Hours are displayed as days (÷8). A third "Totale" row shows the combined budget (vacation + leave) with a vertical marker line indicating the company target position, so the user can see consumed budget relative to both the full total and the company target at a glance.
